Two test failures are my wrong assumptions about the reset config. `0x60A0` → bit5 (AL)=1 and bit9 (TM)=0. Let me verify the decode with a quick calc, then fix the tests:
$ python3 -c "
w=0x60A0
print('bit9/TM', (w>>9)&1, 'bit5/AL', (w>>5)&1, 'CR', (w>>6)&3, 'R', (w>>13)&3, 'F', (w>>11)&3)
print('toWord dropping read-only ->', (w & ~0x0020) & ~0x6000 | 0x6000)
print('0x6080 =', 0x6080, '0x60A0 =', 0x60A0)
"
bit9/TM 0 bit5/AL 1 CR 2 R 3 F 0
toWord dropping read-only -> 24704
0x6080 = 24704 0x60A0 = 24736

Confirmed. Fixing the three wrong
